  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNSCR 1325 Kvinna till Kvinna - Mindefense COL - 1325 Course Kvinna till Kvinna - Mindefense COL</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNSCR 1325 kurs Kvinna till Kvinna - F&#xf6;rsvarsdepartamentet COL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building to the Ministry of Defense and the military forces i Colombia on the United Nations Security Council resolution 1325 on women, peace and security. The contribution aims at strengthening the capacity of the Ministry of Defense, and the several institutions that form part of it, to implement the women, peace and security agenda in terms of both knowledge and tools. The program is built upon four modules encompassing theoretical and practical approaches: 1) Exchange of experiences; 2) Theoretical knowledge - understanding the women, peace and security agenda; 3) Methods and tools for change; 4) Methods and tools to implement the women, peace and security agenda (best practices).
Kvinna till Kvinna will be responsible of the implementation of the contribution, but there will be a strong coordination with the Folke Bernardotte Academy (FBA), The Embassy of Sweden in Bogot&#xe1; and the Ministry of Defense. This will be done during all the stages of the contribution.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos F&#xf6;rsvarsministeriet, och de institutioner som utg&#xf6;r en del av det, att implementera agendan f&#xf6;r kvinnor, fred och s&#xe4;kerhet avseende b&#xe5;de kunskap och verktyg. Programmet &#xe4;r baserat p&#xe5; fyra moduler som t&#xe4;cker teoretiska och praktiska f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llningss&#xe4;tt: 1) Utbyte av erfarenheter; 2) Teoretisk kunskap &#x2013; f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else av agendan f&#xf6;r kvinnor, fred och s&#xe4;kerhet; 3) Metoder och redskap f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring; 4) Metoder och verktyg f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra agendan f&#xf6;r kvinnor, fred och s&#xe4;kerhet (b&#xe4;sta praxis).
Kvinna till Kvinna kommer att vara ansvariga f&#xf6;r implementeringen av insatsen, men det kommer att ske i stark samverkan med Folke Bernadotteakademin (FBA), Sveriges Ambassad i Bogot&#xe1; och F&#xf6;rsvarsministeriet. Detta kommer att utf&#xf6;ras under alla faser av insatsen.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the intervention is to strengthen the capacity of the Ministry of Defense, the Military Forces and the Police, to implement the women, peace and security agenda (WPS) in terms of knowledge and tools. The program is built upon four modules encompassing theoretical and practical approaches. 1) Exchange of experiences; 2) Theoretical knowledge - understanding the women, peace and security agenda; 3) Methods and tools for change; 4) Methods and tools to implement the WPS agenda (best practices).</narrative>
  </description>
